# Settings for the ster-vis service. After editing:
#   sudo systemctl restart ster-vis
#
# STER_VIS_ARGS is added to: ster-vis depth --live --headless --calibration /etc/ster-vis/stereo.npz
# See every option with: ster-vis depth --help
#
# --width/--height/--focus must match what the calibration was captured with.
# --stream serves the live view at http://<pi-name>.local:8080/ to anyone on
# the network, without a password; remove it to turn the stream off.
STER_VIS_ARGS="--preset pi5 --width 1280 --height 720 --focus 1.0 --stream 8080"

# To also keep depth maps, add for example:
#   --save-dir /var/lib/ster-vis/depth --save-every 5
# At the pi5 preset each map is 640x360, about 0.1 MB; one every 5 s is
# roughly 2 GB a day, so only do this with a plan for clearing them.
